{
  "description": "Health alerts (HealthEvaluator, CPUHistory, HealthSnoozes, NotificationPolicy). Sizes are bytes in decimal units (1 GB = 1000000000); uptime is seconds. evaluate: a snapshot (every field optional; absent = no reading) plus optional cpuSamples -> the issues raised, in order: severity descending (critical, warning, info), then id ascending (ordinal). Thresholds: disk.low critical if free/total < 5% or free < 5 GB, warning if < 10% or < 15 GB (needs both free and total, total > 0); memory.pressure mirrors pressure warning/critical; battery.health (info) if healthPercent < 80; trash.large (info) if trashSize >= 5 GB; uptime.long (info) if uptime > 14 days; cpu.hog:<name> (warning) from cpuSamples. cpuHog: samples are appended in order to an empty history; t is seconds since an arbitrary origin; name/cpu null = no reading. Each append first drops entries older than t - 120 s. A hog is the name that was on top at >= 80% in every kept entry, the entries span >= 110 s, and no gap between consecutive entries is > 20 s; expected is that name or null. snooze: apply snoozes in order (day = +86400 s, week = +604800 s, forever = never ends) then each check is isSnoozed(id, now) = now < until. notify: issues to notify = severity >= warning, not snoozed at now, and never notified or notified >= 6 h (21600 s) ago; expected keeps input order. Dates are ISO-8601 UTC.",
